Three technical controls to add (these would have stopped Target)

MFA on supplier accounts. Target’s HVAC contractor only needed a stolen username and password. With MFA, those stolen credentials alone wouldn’t have been enough.
Network segmentation. Even after the attackers got in through the vendor portal, they shouldn’t have been able to reach the checkout systems. Separating the network into zones keeps a supplier’s area walled off from payments. Think of it as a separate ward with its own locked doors.
